{"reasoning": "Rx-07 should not be dispensed. The prescriber, Dr. R. Hale, has had a lapsed DEA registration since 2026-08-03, so he could not validly prescribe oxycodone 30 mg for a 180-tablet fill on 2026-11-08. The PDMP shows two earlier Hale-prescribed oxycodone 30 mg fills after the lapse (120 on 11-01 at Lakeside, 90 on 11-05 at Corner Drug Co.), which suggests possible prescription fraud or doctor-shopping. The Rx-07 entry was made at 23:41, after the 21:00 close, and the audit log shows no outbound verification call, despite a note marking the verification 'done'. The weekly count also shows an unexplained oxycodone 30 mg shortfall of 240 tablets, adjusted as a 'miscount' by J. Ortiz, who also entered Rx-07 and Rx-03. These facts point to possible diversion, so the matter needs pharmacist review and reporting to DEA Diversion and the State Board. Rx-03 and Rx-06 have logged verification calls that match the phone records, and the other Rx lines have active prescribers, so I am approving the rest of the batch with Rx-07 excluded. The 240-tablet loss may also be reportable on DEA Form 106 within one business day of discovery, which the pharmacist-in-charge needs to decide promptly.",
